WEBVTT

NOTE Narration by an AI voice: Matilda (XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX), eleven_v4.

intro
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.820
Here, Cursor CLI builds a Splunk dashboard from one plain-language prompt on a real Splunk Cloud stack.

health
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.480
A quick splunkctl check first. The stack is green.

ask
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:25.560
The prompt asks for four panels, from p95 latency to latency by region, then a deploy and a check that every panel renders.

plan
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.580
Now Cursor plans the work.

skills
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:38.500
Cursor loads Agent Skills for Dashboard Studio and splunkctl, so it follows Splunk's conventions instead of guessing.

discover
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:46.400
Through the Splunk MCP Server, it finds the checkout index, samples the fields, and tests each search.

numbers
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:56.680
p95 latency is about 480 milliseconds, and half a percent of requests fail with a server error.

real-data
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:04.000
That's the difference from a template. Every panel starts from a search that already returned real data.

existing
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:11.700
It also lists the dashboards already in Splunk, to match how they're stored before writing its own.

write
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.080
With the data confirmed, it writes the Dashboard Studio definition.

gate
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.640
Deploying is a write, so splunkctl stops it and waits for your approval.

deploy
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:34.920
Approved. Cursor reruns the same command with your go-ahead, and the dashboard is created.

render
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:43.100
Next, it opens the dashboard in Splunk Web with Playwright and checks all four panels.

read-page
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:52.160
Instead of eyeballing a screenshot, it reads the live page and checks each panel for real values, not an empty chart.

regions
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.940
Region names in the bar chart prove the last panel has data too.

result
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.220
Every panel renders, with the numbers it found in the data.

outro
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:13.620
A final shell check confirms the dashboard is live. One prompt, one approval, and a verified dashboard.
